      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. i ran it through our tool and it's okay, but the score is actually pretty low—only about 65% of the words are under 3 syllables. \n\nit's clear why, you used words like \"condition,\" \"managing,\" and \"hypertension\" which are dragging the score down. i know i said don't game it, but we really need this to be much easier to scan for people who are having trouble reading. \n\ncan you try a second draft? try to get that score up significantly by using shorter, punchier words, but please keep the medical meaning intact. don't lose the nuance of why the pressure in the arteries is a risk, just... try to say it more simply.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
